plication\n\nDiabetic ketoacidosis (DKA) is a serious metabolic condition that can arise from poorly managed diabetes, particularly in patients with insufficient insulin levels. It is characterized by high levels of ketones and elevated blood sugar, necessitating prompt medical intervention. The risk of DKA underscores the importance of effective insulin management and monitoring in diabetic patients. The interplay between insulin therapy and the prevention of DKA is crucial for maintaining patient health and avoiding life-threatening complications [Data: Entities (4190, 2072); Relationships (3264, 1633, 8801)].\n\n## Nutritional management in burn patients\n\nPatients who have suffered severe burns require specialized nutritional management due to their hypermetabolic state. This community highlights the importance of enteral and parenteral nutrition in supporting recovery and preventing malnutrition in these vulnerable patients. Insulin plays a significant role in managing blood glucose levels in burn patients, as they are at high risk for hyperglycemia. The relationship between nutritional support and insulin therapy is essential for optimizing recovery outcomes in burn patients [Data: Entities (2303, 4261); Relationships (4800, 2768, 8815)].\n\n## Interactions between medications and nutrition\n\nThe interactions between medications (fármacos) and nutrition are critical in clinical settings, particularly for patients receiving enteral nutrition. Certain medications can affect gastrointestinal function, which in turn impacts the absorption and efficacy of nutritional support. Understanding these interactions is vital for optimizing treatment outcomes and ensuring patient safety, especially in complex cases involving diabetes and burn management [Data: Entities (144, 14199); Relationships (1772, 2821, 811)].\n\n## The role of nutritional formulas for diabetic patients\n\nNutritional formulas designed for diabetic patients are essential for meeting their dietary needs, particularly when managing blood glucose levels. These formulas often incorporate modified carbohydrates and increased fat content to better align with the metabolic requirements of diabetic individuals. The relationship between insulin management and the use of specialized nutritional formulas is crucial for effective diabetes care [Data: Entities (2375, 5673); Relationships (5657, 8811)].", "# Duodenopancreatectomy and Associated Surgical Complications\n\nThis community focuses on the surgical procedure of duodenopancreatectomy and its related complications, particularly anastomotic dehiscence. Key entities include the ERAS Society, which provides guidelines for perioperative care, and various surgical procedures and conditions associated with pancreatic cancer treatment.\n\n## Duodenopancreatectomy as a critical surgical intervention\n\nDuodenopancreatectomy is a significant surgical procedure primarily used in the treatment of pancreatic diseases, particularly pancreatic cancer. This operation involves the removal of the duodenum and part of the pancreas, which can lead to serious complications such as diabetes and malabsorption. The complexity of this surgery necessitates careful management and adherence to best practices to ensure patient safety and recovery. The procedure's importance in surgical oncology highlights its role in addressing life-threatening conditions. [Data: Entities (5022, 6558); Relationships (14515, 597)]\n\n## Anastomotic dehiscence as a major complication\n\nAnastomotic dehiscence is a significant complication that can occur after duodenopancreatectomy, indicating a failure of the surgical connection between intestinal segments. This condition can lead to severe patient outcomes, including infection and the need for further surgical intervention. Understanding the risk factors and management strategies for anastomotic dehiscence is crucial for improving surgical outcomes and patient care. The relationship between duodenopancreatectomy and anastomotic dehiscence underscores the need for vigilance in postoperative care. [Data: Entities (5027); Relationships (14513, 12205)]\n\n## Role of the ERAS Society in enhancing surgical recovery\n\nThe ERAS Society plays a vital role in improving perioperative care through its guidelines aimed at optimizing recovery following surgeries like duodenopancreatectomy. By providing evidence-based recommendations, the ERAS Society helps healthcare professionals implement best practices that can lead to better patient outcomes. Their focus on enhancing recovery protocols is particularly important for complex surgeries, where recovery can be significantly impacted by the quality of perioperative care. [Data: Entities (5023); Relationships (14511)]\n\n## Nutritional considerations post-duodenopancreatectomy\n\nNutritional management is a critical aspect of care for patients undergoing duodenopancreatectomy. Both enteral and parenteral nutrition strategies are considered based on the patient's condition and recovery status. Enteral nutrition is recommended to ensure adequate nutrient intake, while parenteral nutrition may be necessary when enteral feeding is not feasible. These nutritional strategies are essential for preventing complications and promoting recovery in patients post-surgery. [Data: Relationships (4748, 2689)]\n\n## K. Lassen's contributions to perioperative care\n\nK. Lassen is recognized for his contributions to the guidelines provided by the ERAS Society, particularly in the context of perioperative care for pancreatic surgeries. His research in clinical nutrition is significant for developing protocols that enhance recovery and minimize complications for patients undergoing complex surgical procedures. The involvement of experts like Lassen in guideline development underscores the importance of evidence-based practices in surgical care. [Data: Entities (5024); Relationships (14516)]", "# Nutritional Support Community: Hospital La Fe and Related Condi